\subsubsection*{2.4 Pipelines}

Individual lazy tools compose into larger lazy pipelines. Each stage
pulls from the stage before it, and \texttt{islice} or \texttt{take}
terminates an otherwise infinite chain.

Common shapes: \texttt{islice(map(f, xs), n)},
\texttt{sum(islice(chain(a, b), n))}, \texttt{take(filter(p, xs), n)}.
The same principles apply no matter how many stages the pipeline has.
